# Mobile Layout

Portal is **mobile-first** and installable as a PWA. Respect the phone chrome (notch, Dynamic Island, home indicator) and the bottom tab bar.

## Viewport

Portal / admin shell pages:

```html
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover">
```

`viewport-fit=cover` is required for `env(safe-area-inset-*)` to work on iPhone.

## Breakpoints (project convention)

| Width | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `< 640px` | Phone — single column, touch targets |
| `< 768px` | Mobile shell — bottom tab bar, hide desktop sidebar |
| `≥ 768px` | Desktop shell — sidebar, hide bottom tabs |
| `≥ 1024px` | Wide layouts / multi-column where useful |

Prefer mobile-first: base styles for phone, then `@media (min-width: …)`.

## Safe areas

Use CSS env vars — never hard-code notch/home-indicator height:

- `env(safe-area-inset-top)`
- `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)`
- `env(safe-area-inset-left)` / `right` when full-bleed edge UI needs it

Examples:

```css
padding-top: max(1rem, env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px));
padding-bottom: calc(72px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
```

Fixed top chrome (mobile header) and fixed bottom chrome (tab bar / drawer) must include the matching inset.

## Bottom tab bar

- Portal pages with shell: `body` class `has-bottom-bar`
- On `max-width: 767px`, `.has-bottom-bar` adds bottom padding for the tab bar + home indicator (`css/shared.css`)
- Tab bar itself pads with `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)`
- Do **not** put primary CTAs under the tab bar without extra clearance

## Shell checklist (portal pages)

- [ ] `viewport-fit=cover`
- [ ] `has-bottom-bar` when using pageShell tabs
- [ ] `#nav-placeholder`, `#footer-placeholder`, `#tabs-placeholder`
- [ ] Content not trapped under notch or dock
- [ ] Touch targets ≥ ~44px where possible
- [ ] No hover-only critical actions on mobile

## Anti-patterns

- Missing `viewport-fit=cover` then using safe-area env vars
- Fixed `bottom: 0` buttons that ignore tab bar + home indicator
- Desktop-only hover menus with no tap equivalent
- Horizontal overflow from fixed widths / large grids without wrapping
